    "details": "PowerDNS Team reports:\n\n> CVE ID: CVE-2026-73206\\\n> \\\n> A malicious server can send a crafted reply that leads to high\n> resource utilization decompression name pointers in DNS packets.\\\n> \\\n> This is a multi-vendor issue. Multiple DNS vendors are releasing fixed\n> version of their products.\\\n> \\\n> The remedy is: upgrade to a patched version. The patched version\n> imposes limits on the number of decompression done for a single name\n> and for a DNS packet as a whole.\n",
